{
  "plugin": "@vectorize-io/hindsight-coding-agents",
  "version": "0.8.6",
  "note": "Request shapes as the plugin's one HTTP client class sends them, transcribed by hand from its published bundle. No plugin code is vendored. Every URL is apiUrl + /v1/default/banks/ + encodeURIComponent(bank) + suffix, with Authorization: Bearer <apiToken> and no other custom header. Ids, text, the configured stamp tag and the mission and strategy bodies of the bank template are made up or abbreviated; field names and fixed values are the plugin's. 'path' is relative to apiUrl. 'expect.status' is what hal0's endpoint answers; 'expect.engine' is the engine call it makes, or null when it makes none. In 'expect.engine', a document is named by the id hal0 stores it under for the bridge client 'cc' in project 'hal0' (<project>::<client>::<id>), and '{engine operation id}' stands for the id hal0 derives from the client and the operation id in the request. The knowledge-base cases run against a platform bank whose tree holds the folder 'project:hal0' (id kf-hal0) with a folder 'Initiatives' (kf-initiatives) and a page 'Component map' (kp-architecture) that client 'cc' wrote through this endpoint.",
  "requests": [
    {
      "name": "version_probe",
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/version",
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "engine": "GET /version"
      }
    },
